        "parms": "# bendin, xbendin, touchin and polyin — the wheel and pressure\nThe pitch wheel sends pitch bend. bendin reports it at 7 bits, 0-127 with 64 at rest, as Max's does. xbendin reports all 14 bits, 0-16383 with 8192 at rest, and xbendin2 the same as its two bytes: coarse, then fine. Pressing a key harder once it is down sends aftertouch: touchin reports one pressure for the whole channel, polyin a pressure per key.\nThe first argument is the input port, counted from 0; the midiinfo tutorial lists them. A port that cannot be opened, or no keyboard at all, leaves the object silent, and the patch still loads. On Windows a port can be open in one place at a time, so untick it under Settings › MIDI for a patch to hear it. The second argument is a channel, 1-16, or 0 for all.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
